      "title": "Inline PDF viewer — a pinned pdf.js, installed at build time",
      "description": "Show a published PDF inside a generated page — search, scroll, jump to page, print and download — with the pinned pdf.js viewer the site build installs. Which two Tools do it, the publication-gate rule that decides whether a page may embed a document at all, why the viewer opens only allowlisted hosts, and the three pdf.js behaviours that were measured rather than assumed. Read before putting a PDF on a page, before bumping the pdf.js pin, and when an embedded viewer shows an empty frame.",
